    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d646">

                <pb facs="1496" n="1480" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg1480"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">455.006/9–451: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in Belgium
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-09-08T13:00:00-04:00">September 8,
                            1951—1 p. m</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>315. Re Embtel 301, para A–2, if QRs on US goods contemplated, Emb shld remind
                    Belgians their GATT obligations. QRs must conform requirements GATT Arts
                        XII–2(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) and XIV–1(<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >b</hi>). Also Art XII–4(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) requires that prior
                    to (or, if impracticable, immediately after) imposition new restrictions CP’s
                    must be consulted re balance payments difficulties, alternative measures,
                    possible effect such measures on other CP’s. We think Belg wld be well advised
                    initiate consultations if QRs contemplated since if they do not others may at
                    Sixth Session.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d646-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d646-f1" n="1" xml:id="d646-f1-content">
                <p>For documentation regarding the problem of quantitative restrictions within the
                    framework of the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade (GATT) and the United
                    States position relating thereto, see <ref target="frus1950v01#pg_692">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1950, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, pp. 692</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
